-- Step 22: selling at the counter to a walk-in buyer, who pays at once.
-- track: A
--
-- The CREATE TABLE / constraint statements are generated by drizzle-kit from
-- src/modules/counter-sales/schema.ts. The sections marked "hand-written" are not managed by
-- Drizzle. Reverse with the file of the same name in drizzle/down.
--
-- Each company has one customer that stands for every walk-in buyer, made the first time it is
-- needed by app.walk_in_customer(): unregistered, no credit days, no credit limit. A counter
-- sale is made by the app in one transaction from what is already there:
--
--   a sales order to the walk-in customer, written as a draft with a counter_sales row that
--   holds the buyer's name and phone as typed, then submitted (SO-);
--   its invoice, made straight from the order and posted, which takes the goods out of stock
--   and puts the sale in the books (SI-);
--   a cash or bank receipt for the invoice's total, set against it in full and posted (RC-).
--
-- The buyer's name goes onto the order and the invoice (and onto a later credit note) as each
-- is submitted, in place of the walk-in customer's name, so screens, prints and journals name
-- the buyer.
--
-- A walk-in buyer gets no credit, and the walk-in customer is sold to in no other way: the
-- database refuses a quotation or a delivery note to it, an order or an invoice to it that is
-- not a counter sale's, and a receipt from it that is not the counter sale's own (cash or bank,
-- paying that invoice in full). A return is a credit note, as for any invoice; what it leaves
-- the walk-in customer is refunded when refunds exist (Step 34).
--
-- Database error codes of this track are SE100 to SE199 (docs/PARALLEL.md):
--   SE122  the walk-in customer is sold to only at the counter, and pays at once
--   SE123  a counter sale is written once and never changed or removed

